## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of barriers, memory visibility, and race conditions in low-level concurrent code.

## Key Concepts

- Reusable barrier (sense-reversing)
- Atomic memory orders (acq_rel, acquire, release, relaxed)
- ABA avoidance via generation/sense flip
- Spin-wait considerations and _mm_pause() usage

## Code Example

```c
typedef struct {
  int N;
  _Atomic int count;
  _Atomic int sense;
} barrier_t;

void barrier_init(barrier_t *b, int N){
  b->N = N;
  atomic_init(&b->count, N);
  atomic_init(&b->sense, 0);
}

void barrier_wait(barrier_t *b){
  int local = !atomic_load_explicit(&b->sense, memory_order_relaxed);
  if (atomic_fetch_sub_explicit(&b->count, 1, memory_order_acq_rel) == 1){
    atomic_store_explicit(&b->count, b->N, memory_order_relaxed);
    atomic_store_explicit(&b->sense, local, memory_order_release);
  } else {
    while (atomic_load_explicit(&b->sense, memory_order_acquire) != local) {
      _mm_pause();
    }
  }
}
```

